meta {
  name: deactivate admin
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

delete {
  url: {{base_url}}/administrator/admins/:id/
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: 1f4b8c02-7d63-4a19-8e50-2c9f7b3d1a86
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  **Master admin only.** Deactivates rather than deletes: sets `active` false on
  the profile and `is_active` false on the login, so the row survives. Blog posts
  reference their author, and deleting would orphan them.

  A master cannot deactivate their own account -- that returns 400.

  There is no reactivate endpoint; `PATCH` with `{"active": true}` does it,
  though that leaves `User.is_active` false, so set the password again via
  `password_txt` to fully restore access.

  ## API example response
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Admin deactivated."
  }
}
